<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  One more view tag declared as a real id resource, for the same reason values/ids.xml
  gives: setTag(Object) with no key clobbers whatever else stored a tag on that view,
  and an id resource is the only key aapt guarantees is unique. It lives in its own
  file rather than in ids.xml because it belongs to view_row.xml's trailing slot, the
  way values/tokens_row_action.xml's dimens do.
-->
<resources>
    <!-- WHICH GLYPH @id/row_icon_action's TouchDelegate WAS MEASURED FOR, or absent
         when it has none yet.

         RowBinder shrinks that button to @dimen/row_action_size so its ink can reach
         the gutter, and gives the 48dp back with View.expandTouchTarget. That helper
         registers a delegate on the PARENT and is documented «call it ONCE per view —
         from onCreateViewHolder, never onBindViewHolder»: a View holds one delegate,
         the composite that shares it only ever grows, and RowBinder.bind runs on every
         bind of a row five adapters recycle. Without a stamp on the view itself, a
         list scrolled for a minute would carry a thousand identical delegates and
         offer the touch to each one.

         It stores the ICON and not a flag because the two glyphs park the box 6.25dp
         apart, so a row recycled from «копировать» to «⋮» has earned a second rect.
         Both point at the same button, so the stale one only ever widens its target. -->
    <item name="tag_row_action_touch" type="id" />
</resources>
